prompt:
Write an accessible star-rating input in TypeScript (strict mode) for React 19 and export it as

```ts
export function StarRating(props: {
  value: number;
  onChange: (v: number) => void;
  max?: number;
  readOnly?: boolean;
}): React.ReactElement
```

It is controlled: it shows `value` and reports changes through `onChange`; it never changes what it shows on its own.

Markup and ARIA:
- An element with `role="radiogroup"` whose accessible name is `Rating`, and that can take keyboard focus (`tabIndex={0}`).
- Inside it, one element with `role="radio"` per star, `max` stars in total (`max` defaults to `5`), in order. Star n's accessible name is `1 star` for n = 1 and `n stars` otherwise (`2 stars`, `3 stars`, ...).
- Star n has `aria-checked="true"` when n equals `value` and `aria-checked="false"` otherwise (so with `value` 0 no star is checked).
- When `readOnly` is set, every star has `aria-disabled="true"`.

Behaviour (when `readOnly` is not set):
- Clicking star n calls `onChange(n)`.
- While the radiogroup has focus, ArrowRight calls `onChange(value + 1)` and ArrowLeft calls `onChange(value - 1)`, kept within 1..`max`: at the boundary (ArrowRight at `max`, ArrowLeft at 1) `onChange` is not called. From `value` 0, ArrowRight calls `onChange(1)`.

When `readOnly` is set, clicks and keys never call `onChange`.

You may import only `react`. Answer with a single ```tsx code block containing only the module.
